{"assertions":[{"answerability":"answerable","basis":"The New American Bible, Revised Edition introduction says that no individual psalm can be dated securely and that none is as late as the Maccabean period, around 165 B.C.","basis_class":"catholic-critical","boundary":{"direction":"before","endpoint":"165 B.C.","statement":"before c. 165 B.C."},"date":"before c. 165 B.C.","derived":false,"disposition":"preferred","inherited":true,"label":"before the Maccabean period, around 165 B.C.; no individual psalm can be dated securely","note":"The endpoint is the source's approximate historical horizon, not an exact composition year. The claim says only \"before\" that horizon and preserves the source's refusal to date an individual psalm securely.","precision":"boundary","profile":"catholic-critical-v1","relation":"composition","reporting_exception":null,"scope":"Ps","sources":["passage.united-states-conference-of-catholic-bishops.new-american-bible-revised-edition.english-usccb-web-2026-07-28.psalms-introduction"],"subject":"critical.psalms.latest-composition-boundary","title":"The latest composition boundary shared by the Psalms"}],"chronology_status":"composition-only","locus":"Ps.144.2","reason":"","requested_profile":"catholic-comprehensive-v1","resolved_profiles":{"composition":"catholic-critical-v1"},"status":"ok","v":1}
